1
00:33:21,315 --> 00:33:23,745
Oh, it's a first edition
and you've signed it.

2
00:33:23,775 --> 00:33:26,702
- Yes, of course.
- Thank you so much.

3
00:33:28,634 --> 00:33:31,938
- May I serve tea now Miss Van Gorder?
- Yes, please do Warner.

4
00:33:31,968 --> 00:33:32,979
Thank you.

5
00:33:34,911 --> 00:33:38,260
- I see you've engaged new servants.
- Yes, of course.

6
00:33:38,290 --> 00:33:40,644
Oh, how did you persuade
them to live in this house?

7
00:33:41,112 --> 00:33:44,839
Jane Patterson, my new housekeeper,
knows this house better than you do doctor.

8
00:33:44,869 --> 00:33:49,486
She worked for John Fleming
and Warner was my chauffeur.

9
00:33:50,949 --> 00:33:53,680
- Chauffeur turned butler?
- It's incredible.

10
00:33:53,967 --> 00:33:56,200
He can play any part at a moment's notice.

11
00:33:56,562 --> 00:33:59,007
Ah, did you, did you get a plumber Warner?

12
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:01,693
No, we can't get a
plumber for three days madame.

13
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:05,993
What about that leaking pipe? The
basement will be flooded in three days.

14
00:34:06,023 --> 00:34:07,985
The pipe is no longer leaking.

15
00:34:08,603 --> 00:34:11,123
You mean it's dried up of its own accord?

16
00:34:11,153 --> 00:34:14,306
No, not quite, I packed the elbow
where the water was coming up.

17
00:34:14,775 --> 00:34:16,495
Packed the elbow?

18
00:34:17,008 --> 00:34:21,534
- Where did you learn how to do that?
- Into each life, a little rain must fall.

19
00:34:21,564 --> 00:34:23,902
And a careful man
learns to keep himself dry.

20
00:34:24,174 --> 00:34:26,634
Now, is there anything that
you require Miss Van Gorder?

21
00:34:26,664 --> 00:34:29,651
- No, not at the moment Warner.
- Thank you madame.

22
00:34:31,476 --> 00:34:33,679
Now, there's a character.

23
00:34:34,720 --> 00:34:37,194
How long did you say that he
worked for you as chauffeur?

24
00:34:37,587 --> 00:34:38,658
About three months.

25
00:34:38,688 --> 00:34:41,027
Well, I hope he doesn't
have a police record.

26
00:34:42,838 --> 00:34:44,015
My dear Dale...

27
00:34:44,045 --> 00:34:47,396
it may interest you to know that
the last night of his life, John Fleming...

28
00:34:47,426 --> 00:34:50,243
told me that he loved
your husband like a son.

29
00:34:51,073 --> 00:34:55,615
If Fleming were alive today, he would
be fighting to prove Vick's innocence.

30
00:34:56,988 --> 00:34:59,342
Could Mr. Fleming prove his own innocence?

31
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:03,430
Miss Van Gorder,
can there be any doubt about it?

32
00:35:04,350 --> 00:35:07,896
There will be when
Miss Holland testifies at Vick's trial.

33
00:35:08,877 --> 00:35:09,873
Oh?

34
00:35:10,582 --> 00:35:13,298
You know something
that we haven't heard yet Judie?

35
00:35:13,871 --> 00:35:16,964
Something I saw with my own eyes.

36
00:35:17,809 --> 00:35:20,072
She's not permitted to say what it was.

37
00:35:20,299 --> 00:35:22,592
My dear girl, I wouldn't
think of asking her.

38
00:35:23,362 --> 00:35:26,749
But let's assume for a moment
that Fleming did steal the million, now...

39
00:35:26,779 --> 00:35:28,718
what would he do about it? Where is it?

40
00:35:29,488 --> 00:35:32,928
Hidden some place where he could lay his hands
on it without getting caught in the act.

41
00:35:34,392 --> 00:35:38,270
Now, if I was writing this
instead of living in the middle of it...

42
00:35:39,130 --> 00:35:41,740
I'd hide it right
here in this spooky old house.

43
00:35:42,102 --> 00:35:45,255
Under a loose floorboard or up a chimney?

44
00:35:46,704 --> 00:35:48,635
If Mr. Fleming...

45
00:35:48,861 --> 00:35:53,086
had the nerve to steal a million,
he'd make his plans well in advance.

46
00:35:54,157 --> 00:35:56,525
I'd say he'd prepare a place to hide it.

47
00:35:57,641 --> 00:36:00,387
Possibly when this house was being built.

48
00:36:01,565 --> 00:36:04,718
I rented this place from
Mark Fleming, his nephew.

49
00:36:04,960 --> 00:36:09,139
I wonder, I wonder if
he had the floor plans.

50
00:36:09,637 --> 00:36:12,263
- I'll ask him.
- Yes.

51
00:36:12,293 --> 00:36:15,491
Lizzie, will you bring
Miss Bailey the phone?
